IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Part 12, Division 3 (insider trading), second part: ss 218 to 221 (connected persons, other persons, intention to use, penalties).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Reading an answer and the markers are explained at the head of sfab-division-1.l4 and in NOTES.md.
-- A bare "where" gate (s 218(1), s 219(1)) answers JUST FALSE when it fails, by the Guide's periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b); each such branch is marked.
--
-- WHICH "connected person". Section 218(5) defines "connected person" for this Division itself ("In this Division"). It is not the term of s 2(1)
-- (the relatives and 20%-controlled bodies of an individual), so no keel function is called: the Division's own definition is encoded here.
-- A caller who would ask "is this person connected" passes the answer under section 218(5)(b) into ss 218(1), 218(1A) and 219(1).

DECLARE `s 218 to s 219 prohibited act` IS ONE OF
    `s 218(2) subscribe for, purchase or sell the securities, contracts or units, or enter into an agreement to, or procure another person to, while connected to the corporation and in possession of inside information`
    `s 218(3) communicate, or cause to be communicated, inside information to another person who would be likely to subscribe for, purchase or sell, or procure a third person to`
    `s 219(2) subscribe for, purchase or sell the securities, contracts or units, or enter into an agreement to, or procure another person to, while in possession of inside information as an insider`
    `s 219(3) communicate, or cause to be communicated, inside information to another person who would be likely to subscribe for, purchase or sell, or procure a third person to`

§ `s 218(5) and (6): who is a connected person`

-- src:35415 | (6) In subsection (5), “officer”, in relation to a corporation,
-- src:35416 | includes —
-- src:35418 | (a) a director, secretary or employee of the corporation;
-- src:35420 | (b) a receiver, or receiver and manager, of property of the
-- src:35421 | corporation;
-- src:35423 | (c) a judicial manager of the corporation;
-- src:35425 | (d) a liquidator of the corporation; and
-- src:35427 | (e) a trustee or other person administering a compromise or
-- src:35428 | arrangement made between the corporation and another
-- src:35429 | person.
@ref s 218(6) (src:35415-35429)
GIVEN
    `the person is a director, secretary or employee of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a director, secretary or employee of the corporation?
    `the person is a receiver, or receiver and manager, of property of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a receiver, or receiver and manager, of property of the corporation?
    `the person is a judicial manager of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a judicial manager of the corporation?
    `the person is a liquidator of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a liquidator of the corporation?
    `the person is a trustee or other person administering a compromise or arrangement made between the corporation and another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a trustee or other person administering a compromise or arrangement made between the corporation and another person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 218(6) the person is an officer of the corporation for the purposes of subsection (5)` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director, secretary or employee of the corporation` OR `the person is a receiver, or receiver and manager, of property of the corporation` OR `the person is a judicial manager of the corporation` OR `the person is a liquidator of the corporation` OR `the person is a trustee or other person administering a compromise or arrangement made between the corporation and another person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“officer”, in relation to a corporation, includes"

-- src:35388 | (b) a person is connected to a corporation if —
-- src:35390 | (i) the person is an officer of that corporation or of a
-- src:35391 | related corporation;
-- src:35393 | (ii) the person is a substantial shareholder in that
-- src:35394 | corporation or in a related corporation; or
-- src:35396 | (iii) the person occupies a position that may reasonably
-- src:35397 | be expected to give the person access to information
-- src:35398 | of a kind to which this section applies by virtue of —
-- src:35400 | (A) any professional or business relationship
-- src:35401 | existing between the person (or the person’s
-- src:35402 | employer or a corporation of which the person
-- src:35407 | is an officer) and that corporation or a related
-- src:35408 | corporation; or
-- src:35410 | (B) being an officer of a substantial shareholder in
-- src:35411 | that corporation or in a related corporation.
@ref s 218(5)(b) (src:35388-35411)
GIVEN
    `the person is an officer of the corporation or of a related corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an officer of the corporation or of a related corporation (reading "officer" as section 218(6) does)?
    `the person is a substantial shareholder in the corporation or in a related corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a substantial shareholder in the corporation or in a related corporation?
    `the person occupies a position that may reasonably be expected to give the person access to information of a kind to which section 218 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person occupy a position that may reasonably be expected to give the person access to information of a kind to which section 218 applies?
    `that access is by virtue of a professional or business relationship between the corporation or a related corporation and the person, the person's employer or a corporation of which the person is an officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that access by virtue of a professional or business relationship existing between the person (or the person's employer or a corporation of which the person is an officer) and the corporation or a related corporation?
    `that access is by virtue of being an officer of a substantial shareholder in the corporation or in a related corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that access by virtue of being an officer of a substantial shareholder in the corporation or in a related corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 218(5)(b) the person is connected to the corporation` MEANS
    IF `the person is an officer of the corporation or of a related corporation` OR `the person is a substantial shareholder in the corporation or in a related corporation` OR (`the person occupies a position that may reasonably be expected to give the person access to information of a kind to which section 218 applies` AND (`that access is by virtue of a professional or business relationship between the corporation or a related corporation and the person, the person's employer or a corporation of which the person is an officer` OR `that access is by virtue of being an officer of a substantial shareholder in the corporation or in a related corporation`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person is connected to a corporation if" -- MARGINAL-READING (a)

-- src:35382 | (5) In this Division —
-- src:35384 | (a) “connected person” means a person referred to in
-- src:35385 | subsection (1) or (1A) who is connected to a
-- src:35386 | corporation; and
@ref s 218(5)(a) (src:35382-35386)
GIVEN
    `the person is a person referred to in subsection (1) or (1A) of section 218` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a person referred to in section 218(1) or (1A)?
    `the person is connected to the corporation (the answer under section 218(5)(b))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 218(5)(b) answer for this person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 218(5)(a) the person is a connected person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is a person referred to in subsection (1) or (1A) of section 218`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“connected person” means a person referred to in subsection (1) or (1A)"
        IF `the person is connected to the corporation (the answer under section 218(5)(b))` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is connected is not answered
        OTHERWISE `the person is connected to the corporation (the answer under section 218(5)(b))`

§ `s 218(1) to (4B): the connected person's conditions, bars and presumptions`

-- src:35172 | 218.—(1) Subject to this Division, where —
-- src:35174 | (a) a person who is connected to a corporation possesses
-- src:35175 | information concerning that corporation that is not
-- src:35176 | generally available but, if the information were generally
-- src:35177 | available, a reasonable person would expect it to have a
-- src:35178 | material effect on the price or value of securities or
-- src:35179 | securities‑based derivatives contracts of that corporation;
-- src:35180 | and
-- src:35182 | (b) the connected person knows or ought reasonably to know
-- src:35183 | that —
-- src:35185 | (i) the information is not generally available; and
-- src:35187 | (ii) if it were generally available, it might have a material
-- src:35188 | effect on the price or value of those securities or
-- src:35189 | securities‑based derivatives contracts of that
-- src:35190 | corporation,
-- src:35192 | subsections (2), (3), (4), (5) and (6) apply.
@ref s 218(1) (src:35172-35192)
GIVEN
    `the person is connected to the corporation (the answer under section 218(5)(b))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 218(5)(b) answer for this person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `the person possesses information concerning the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person possess information concerning the corporation?
    `the information is generally available (the answer under section 215)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 215 answer for this information? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `a reasonable person would expect the information, if generally available, to have a material effect on the price or value of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of the corporation (the answer under section 216)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 216 answer for this information, read for securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of the corporation? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `the connected person knows or ought reasonably to know that the information is not generally available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the connected person know, or ought the connected person reasonably to know, that the information is not generally available?
    `the connected person knows or ought reasonably to know that, if generally available, the information might have a material effect on the price or value of those securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the connected person know, or ought the connected person reasonably to know, that, if it were generally available, the information might have a material effect on the price or value of those securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of the corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 218(1) subsections (2), (3), (4), (5) and (6) apply to the connected person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person possesses information concerning the corporation`) OR (`the person is connected to the corporation (the answer under section 218(5)(b))` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`the information is generally available (the answer under section 215)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`a reasonable person would expect the information, if generally available, to have a material effect on the price or value of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of the corporation (the answer under section 216)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (NOT `the connected person knows or ought reasonably to know that the information is not generally available`) OR (NOT `the connected person knows or ought reasonably to know that, if generally available, the information might have a material effect on the price or value of those securities or securities-based derivatives contracts`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to this Division, where" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [WHERE]
        IF (`the person is connected to the corporation (the answer under section 218(5)(b))` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the information is generally available (the answer under section 215)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`a reasonable person would expect the information, if generally available, to have a material effect on the price or value of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of the corporation (the answer under section 216)` EQUALS NOTHING)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb answered by section 215, 216 or 218(5)(b) was not answered
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 218(1) (src:35172-35192)
GIVEN
    `subsections (2), (3), (4), (5) and (6) apply under section 218(1) (the answer under section 218(1))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 218(1) answer for this person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `subsections (2), (3), (4A), (5) and (6) apply under section 218(1A) (the answer under section 218(1A))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 218(1A) answer for this person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 218 subsection (2) and (3) apply to the person under subsection (1) or (1A)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`subsections (2), (3), (4), (5) and (6) apply under section 218(1) (the answer under section 218(1))` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`subsections (2), (3), (4A), (5) and (6) apply under section 218(1A) (the answer under section 218(1A))` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`subsections (2), (3), (4), (5) and (6) apply under section 218(1) (the answer under section 218(1))` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`subsections (2), (3), (4A), (5) and (6) apply under section 218(1A) (the answer under section 218(1A))` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to this Division, where" "Subsections (2), (3), (4A), (5) and (6) apply if"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (1) or (1A) was not answered

-- src:35196 | (1A) Subsections (2), (3), (4A), (5) and (6) apply if —
-- src:35198 | (a) a person is connected to —
-- src:35200 | (i) a corporation that is the trustee of, or manages or
-- src:35201 | operates, a business trust; or
-- src:35206 | (ii) a corporation that is the trustee or manager of a
-- src:35207 | collective investment scheme —
-- src:35209 | (A) that invests primarily in real estate and real
-- src:35210 | estate‑related assets specified by the Authority
-- src:35211 | in the Code on Collective Investment Schemes;
-- src:35212 | and
-- src:35214 | (B) all or any units of which are listed on an
-- src:35215 | approved exchange;
-- src:35217 | (b) the connected person possesses —
-- src:35219 | (i) where the person is connected to a corporation
-- src:35220 | mentioned in paragraph (a)(i), any information
-- src:35221 | concerning the corporation or business trust that is
-- src:35222 | not generally available but, if the information were
-- src:35223 | generally available, a reasonable person would
-- src:35224 | expect it to have a material effect on the price or
-- src:35225 | value of securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:35226 | contracts of the corporation or business trust; or
-- src:35228 | (ii) where the person is connected to a corporation
-- src:35229 | mentioned in paragraph (a)(ii), any information
-- src:35230 | concerning the corporation or collective investment
-- src:35231 | scheme that is not generally available but, if the
-- src:35232 | information were generally available, a reasonable
-- src:35233 | person would expect it to have a material effect on
-- src:35234 | the price or value of securities or securities‑based
-- src:35235 | derivatives contracts of the corporation, or the price
-- src:35236 | or value of CIS units in the scheme; and
-- src:35238 | (c) the connected person knows or ought reasonably to know
-- src:35239 | that —
-- src:35241 | (i) the information is not generally available; and
-- src:35243 | (ii) if it were generally available, it might have a material
-- src:35244 | effect on —
-- src:35246 | (A) where the person is connected to a corporation
-- src:35247 | mentioned in paragraph (a)(i), the price or
-- src:35248 | value of securities or securities‑based
-- src:35253 | derivatives contracts of the corporation or
-- src:35254 | business trust; or
-- src:35256 | (B) where the person is connected to a corporation
-- src:35257 | mentioned in paragraph (a)(ii), the price or
-- src:35258 | value of securities or securities‑based
-- src:35259 | derivatives contracts of the corporation, or
-- src:35260 | the price or value of CIS units in the collective
-- src:35261 | investment scheme.
@ref s 218(1A) (src:35196-35261)
GIVEN
    `the corporation is the trustee of, or manages or operates, a business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation the trustee of, or does it manage or operate, a business trust?
    `the corporation is the trustee or manager of a collective investment scheme that invests primarily in real estate and real estate-related assets specified by the Authority in the Code on Collective Investment Schemes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation the trustee or manager of a collective investment scheme that invests primarily in real estate and real estate-related assets specified by the Authority in the Code on Collective Investment Schemes?
    `all or any units of that collective investment scheme are listed on an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all or any of the units of that collective investment scheme listed on an approved exchange?
    `the person is connected to the corporation (the answer under section 218(5)(b))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 218(5)(b) answer for this person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `the person possesses information concerning the corporation, the business trust or the collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person possess information concerning the corporation, the business trust or the collective investment scheme?
    `the information is generally available (the answer under section 215)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 215 answer for this information? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `a reasonable person would expect the information, if generally available, to have a material effect on the price or value of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of the corporation or business trust, or of CIS units in the scheme (the answer under section 216)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 216 answer for this information, read for the securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units concerned? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `the connected person knows or ought reasonably to know that the information is not generally available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the connected person know, or ought the connected person reasonably to know, that the information is not generally available?
    `the connected person knows or ought reasonably to know that, if generally available, the information might have a material effect on the price or value of the securities, contracts or units concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the connected person know, or ought the connected person reasonably to know, that, if it were generally available, the information might have a material effect on the price or value of the securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units concerned?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 218(1A) subsections (2), (3), (4A), (5) and (6) apply to the person connected to a business trust or scheme corporation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the corporation is the trustee of, or manages or operates, a business trust` OR (`the corporation is the trustee or manager of a collective investment scheme that invests primarily in real estate and real estate-related assets specified by the Authority in the Code on Collective Investment Schemes` AND `all or any units of that collective investment scheme are listed on an approved exchange`))) OR (NOT `the person possesses information concerning the corporation, the business trust or the collective investment scheme`) OR (`the person is connected to the corporation (the answer under section 218(5)(b))` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`the information is generally available (the answer under section 215)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`a reasonable person would expect the information, if generally available, to have a material effect on the price or value of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of the corporation or business trust, or of CIS units in the scheme (the answer under section 216)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (NOT `the connected person knows or ought reasonably to know that the information is not generally available`) OR (NOT `the connected person knows or ought reasonably to know that, if generally available, the information might have a material effect on the price or value of the securities, contracts or units concerned`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (2), (3), (4A), (5) and (6) apply if" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [IF]
        IF (`the person is connected to the corporation (the answer under section 218(5)(b))` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the information is generally available (the answer under section 215)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`a reasonable person would expect the information, if generally available, to have a material effect on the price or value of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of the corporation or business trust, or of CIS units in the scheme (the answer under section 216)` EQUALS NOTHING)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb answered by section 215, 216 or 218(5)(b) was not answered
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:35265 | (2) The connected person must not (whether as principal or
-- src:35266 | agent) —
-- src:35268 | (a) subscribe for, purchase or sell, or enter into an agreement
-- src:35269 | to subscribe for, purchase or sell —
-- src:35271 | (i) the securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:35272 | contracts mentioned in subsection (1); or
-- src:35274 | (ii) the securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:35275 | or CIS units mentioned in subsection (1A); or
-- src:35277 | (b) procure another person to subscribe for, purchase or sell, or
-- src:35278 | to enter into an agreement to subscribe for, purchase or
-- src:35279 | sell —
-- src:35281 | (i) the securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:35282 | contracts mentioned in subsection (1); or
-- src:35284 | (ii) the securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:35285 | or CIS units mentioned in subsection (1A).
@ref s 218(2) (src:35265-35285)
GIVEN
    `subsection (2) applies to the person (the answer under section 218(1) or (1A))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 218(1) or (1A) answer for this person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `the connected person subscribed for, purchased or sold, or entered into an agreement to subscribe for, purchase or sell, the securities, contracts or units, whether as principal or agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the connected person (whether as principal or agent) subscribe for, purchase or sell, or enter into an agreement to subscribe for, purchase or sell, the securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units?
    `the connected person procured another person to subscribe for, purchase or sell, or to enter into an agreement to subscribe for, purchase or sell, the securities, contracts or units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the connected person (whether as principal or agent) procure another person to subscribe for, purchase or sell, or to enter into an agreement to subscribe for, purchase or sell, the securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 218(2) the connected person's dealing or procuring contravenes the bar` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `subsection (2) applies to the person (the answer under section 218(1) or (1A))` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to this Division, where" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [WHERE]
        IF `subsection (2) applies to the person (the answer under section 218(1) or (1A))` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether subsection (2) applies was not answered
        IF `the connected person subscribed for, purchased or sold, or entered into an agreement to subscribe for, purchase or sell, the securities, contracts or units, whether as principal or agent` OR `the connected person procured another person to subscribe for, purchase or sell, or to enter into an agreement to subscribe for, purchase or sell, the securities, contracts or units`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The connected person must not (whether as principal or agent)" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN]

@ref s 218(2) (src:35265-35285)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 218 to s 219 prohibited act`
`s 218(2) the connected person must not deal in, or procure dealing in, the securities while in possession of inside information` MEANS
    PARTY Individual "the connected person"
    SHANT `s 218(2) subscribe for, purchase or sell the securities, contracts or units, or enter into an agreement to, or procure another person to, while connected to the corporation and in possession of inside information`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the connected person subscribed for, purchased or sold the securities, contracts or units, or procured another to, while in possession of information that is not generally available (section 218(2))"

