@ref s 218(3) (src:35289-35315)
GIVEN
    `subsection (3) applies to the person (the answer under section 218(1) or (1A))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 218(1) or (1A) answer for this person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `the connected person communicated the information, or caused it to be communicated, directly or indirectly, to another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the connected person, directly or indirectly, communicate the information, or cause it to be communicated, to another person?
    `the connected person knows, or ought reasonably to know, that the other person would or would be likely to deal in or procure dealing in the securities, contracts or units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the connected person know, or ought the connected person reasonably to know, that the other person would or would be likely to subscribe for, purchase or sell, or enter into an agreement to subscribe for, purchase or sell, the securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units, or procure a third person to?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 218(3) the connected person's communication of the information contravenes the bar` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `subsection (3) applies to the person (the answer under section 218(1) or (1A))` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to this Division, where" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [WHERE]
        IF `subsection (3) applies to the person (the answer under section 218(1) or (1A))` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether subsection (3) applies was not answered
        IF NOT `the connected person communicated the information, or caused it to be communicated, directly or indirectly, to another person`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The connected person must not, directly or indirectly, communicate the information" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN]
        IF `the connected person knows, or ought reasonably to know, that the other person would or would be likely to deal in or procure dealing in the securities, contracts or units`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the connected person knows, or ought reasonably to know" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [IF]

@ref s 218(3) (src:35289-35315)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 218 to s 219 prohibited act`
`s 218(3) the connected person must not communicate the inside information to a person likely to deal` MEANS
    PARTY Individual "the connected person"
    SHANT `s 218(3) communicate, or cause to be communicated, inside information to another person who would be likely to subscribe for, purchase or sell, or procure a third person to`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the connected person communicated the information, or caused it to be communicated, to a person the connected person knew or ought reasonably to have known would be likely to deal or procure dealing (section 218(3))"

-- src:35319 | (4) In any proceedings for a contravention of subsection (2) or (3)
-- src:35320 | against a person connected to a corporation referred to in
-- src:35321 | subsection (1), where the prosecution or claimant proves that the
-- src:35322 | connected person was at the material time —
-- src:35324 | (a) in possession of information concerning the corporation to
-- src:35325 | which the person was connected; and
-- src:35327 | (b) the information was not generally available,
-- src:35329 | it is presumed, until the contrary is proved, that the connected person
-- src:35330 | knew at the material time that —
-- src:35332 | (c) the information was not generally available; and
-- src:35334 | (d) if the information were generally available, it might have a
-- src:35335 | material effect on the price or value of securities or
-- src:35336 | securities‑based derivatives contracts of that corporation.
@ref s 218(4) (src:35319-35336)
GIVEN
    `the proceedings are for a contravention of section 218(2) or (3) against a person connected to a corporation referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings for a contravention of section 218(2) or (3) against a person connected to a corporation referred to in section 218(1)?
    `the prosecution or claimant proves that the connected person was at the material time in possession of information concerning the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prosecution or claimant prove that the connected person was at the material time in possession of information concerning the corporation to which the person was connected?
    `the prosecution or claimant proves that the information was not generally available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prosecution or claimant prove that the information was not generally available?
    `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contrary been proved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 218(4) the connected person is presumed to have known that the information was not generally available and might have a material effect` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the proceedings are for a contravention of section 218(2) or (3) against a person connected to a corporation referred to in subsection (1)` AND `the prosecution or claimant proves that the connected person was at the material time in possession of information concerning the corporation` AND `the prosecution or claimant proves that the information was not generally available`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the prosecution or claimant proves that the connected person was at the material time"
        IF `the contrary is proved`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is presumed, until the contrary is proved"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:35342 | (4A) In any proceedings for a contravention of subsection (2) or (3)
-- src:35343 | against a person connected to a corporation mentioned in
-- src:35344 | subsection (1A)(a)(i) or (ii), the presumption in subsection (4B)
-- src:35345 | applies until the contrary is proved, if the prosecution or claimant
-- src:35346 | proves that the connected person was at the material time —
-- src:35348 | (a) in possession of information concerning the corporation,
-- src:35349 | business trust or collective investment scheme, as the case
-- src:35350 | may be; and
-- src:35355 | (b) the information was not generally available.
@ref s 218(4A) (src:35342-35355)
GIVEN
    `the proceedings are for a contravention of section 218(2) or (3) against a person connected to a corporation mentioned in subsection (1A)(a)(i) or (ii)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings for a contravention of section 218(2) or (3) against a person connected to a corporation mentioned in section 218(1A)(a)(i) or (ii)?
    `the prosecution or claimant proves that the connected person was at the material time in possession of information concerning the corporation, business trust or collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prosecution or claimant prove that the connected person was at the material time in possession of information concerning the corporation, business trust or collective investment scheme, as the case may be?
    `the prosecution or claimant proves that the information was not generally available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prosecution or claimant prove that the information was not generally available?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 218(4A) the presumption in subsection (4B) applies` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are for a contravention of section 218(2) or (3) against a person connected to a corporation mentioned in subsection (1A)(a)(i) or (ii)` AND `the prosecution or claimant proves that the connected person was at the material time in possession of information concerning the corporation, business trust or collective investment scheme` AND `the prosecution or claimant proves that the information was not generally available`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the presumption in subsection (4B) applies until the contrary is proved, if the prosecution or claimant proves"

-- src:35361 | (4B) For the purpose of subsection (4A), the presumption is the
-- src:35362 | connected person knew at the material time that —
-- src:35364 | (a) the information was not generally available; and
-- src:35366 | (b) if the information were generally available, it might have a
-- src:35367 | material effect on —
-- src:35369 | (i) where the person is connected to a corporation
-- src:35370 | mentioned in subsection (1A)(a)(i), the price or
-- src:35371 | value of securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:35372 | contracts of the corporation or business trust; or
-- src:35374 | (ii) where the person is connected to a corporation
-- src:35375 | mentioned in subsection (1A)(a)(ii), the price or
-- src:35376 | value of the securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:35377 | contracts of the corporation or the price or value of
-- src:35378 | CIS units in the collective investment scheme.
@ref s 218(4B) (src:35361-35378)
GIVEN
    `the presumption in subsection (4B) applies (the answer under section 218(4A))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 218(4A) answer for this person? (JUST TRUE or NOTHING)
    `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contrary been proved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 218(4B) the connected person is presumed to have known that the information was not generally available and might have a material effect` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the presumption in subsection (4B) applies (the answer under section 218(4A))` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purpose of subsection (4A), the presumption is"
        IF `the contrary is proved`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "applies until the contrary is proved"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `s 219: prohibited conduct by other persons in possession of inside information`

-- src:35434 | 219.—(1) Subject to this Division, where —
-- src:35436 | (a) a person who is not a connected person referred to in
-- src:35437 | section 218 (called in this section the insider) possesses
-- src:35438 | information that is not generally available but, if the
-- src:35439 | information were generally available, a reasonable person
-- src:35440 | would expect it to have a material effect on the price or
-- src:35441 | value of securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:35442 | or CIS units; and
-- src:35444 | (b) the insider knows that —
-- src:35446 | (i) the information is not generally available; and
-- src:35448 | (ii) if it were generally available, it might have a material
-- src:35449 | effect on the price or value of those securities,
-- src:35450 | securities‑based derivatives contracts or CIS units, as
-- src:35451 | the case may be,
-- src:35453 | subsections (2) and (3) apply.
@ref s 219(1) (src:35434-35453)
GIVEN
    `the person is a connected person referred to in section 218 (the answer under section 218(5)(a))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 218(5)(a) answer for this person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `the insider possesses information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the insider possess information?
    `the information is generally available (the answer under section 215)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 215 answer for this information? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `a reasonable person would expect the information, if generally available, to have a material effect on the price or value of securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units (the answer under section 216)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 216 answer for this information, read for the securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units concerned? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `the insider knows that the information is not generally available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the insider know that the information is not generally available?
    `the insider knows that, if generally available, the information might have a material effect on the price or value of those securities, contracts or units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the insider know that, if it were generally available, the information might have a material effect on the price or value of those securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 219(1) subsections (2) and (3) apply to the insider` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the person is a connected person referred to in section 218 (the answer under section 218(5)(a))` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (NOT `the insider possesses information`) OR (`the information is generally available (the answer under section 215)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`a reasonable person would expect the information, if generally available, to have a material effect on the price or value of securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units (the answer under section 216)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (NOT `the insider knows that the information is not generally available`) OR (NOT `the insider knows that, if generally available, the information might have a material effect on the price or value of those securities, contracts or units`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to this Division, where" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [WHERE]
        IF (`the person is a connected person referred to in section 218 (the answer under section 218(5)(a))` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the information is generally available (the answer under section 215)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`a reasonable person would expect the information, if generally available, to have a material effect on the price or value of securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units (the answer under section 216)` EQUALS NOTHING)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb answered by section 215, 216 or 218(5)(a) was not answered
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:35460 | (2) The insider must not (whether as principal or agent) —
-- src:35462 | (a) subscribe for, purchase or sell, or enter into an agreement
-- src:35463 | to subscribe for, purchase or sell, any such securities,
-- src:35464 | securities‑based derivatives contracts or CIS units, as the
-- src:35465 | case may be; or
-- src:35467 | (b) procure another person to subscribe for, purchase or sell, or
-- src:35468 | to enter into an agreement to subscribe for, purchase or sell,
-- src:35469 | any such securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:35470 | or CIS units, as the case may be.
@ref s 219(2) (src:35460-35470)
GIVEN
    `subsections (2) and (3) apply to the insider (the answer under section 219(1))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 219(1) answer for this person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `the insider subscribed for, purchased or sold, or entered into an agreement to subscribe for, purchase or sell, the securities, contracts or units, whether as principal or agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the insider (whether as principal or agent) subscribe for, purchase or sell, or enter into an agreement to subscribe for, purchase or sell, the securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units?
    `the insider procured another person to subscribe for, purchase or sell, or to enter into an agreement to subscribe for, purchase or sell, the securities, contracts or units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the insider (whether as principal or agent) procure another person to subscribe for, purchase or sell, or to enter into an agreement to subscribe for, purchase or sell, the securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 219(2) the insider's dealing or procuring contravenes the bar` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `subsections (2) and (3) apply to the insider (the answer under section 219(1))` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to this Division, where" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [WHERE]
        IF `subsections (2) and (3) apply to the insider (the answer under section 219(1))` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether subsection (2) applies was not answered
        IF `the insider subscribed for, purchased or sold, or entered into an agreement to subscribe for, purchase or sell, the securities, contracts or units, whether as principal or agent` OR `the insider procured another person to subscribe for, purchase or sell, or to enter into an agreement to subscribe for, purchase or sell, the securities, contracts or units`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The insider must not (whether as principal or agent)" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN]

@ref s 219(2) (src:35460-35470)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 218 to s 219 prohibited act`
`s 219(2) the insider must not deal in, or procure dealing in, the securities while in possession of inside information` MEANS
    PARTY Individual "the insider"
    SHANT `s 219(2) subscribe for, purchase or sell the securities, contracts or units, or enter into an agreement to, or procure another person to, while in possession of inside information as an insider`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the insider subscribed for, purchased or sold the securities, contracts or units, or procured another to, while knowing the information was not generally available (section 219(2))"

-- src:35474 | (3) The insider must not, directly or indirectly, communicate the
-- src:35475 | information mentioned in subsection (1), or cause the information to
-- src:35476 | be communicated, to another person if the insider knows, or ought
-- src:35477 | reasonably to know, that the other person would or would be likely
-- src:35478 | to —
-- src:35480 | (a) subscribe for, purchase or sell, or enter into an agreement
-- src:35481 | to subscribe for, purchase or sell, the securities,
-- src:35482 | securities‑based derivatives contracts or CIS units
-- src:35483 | mentioned in subsection (1); or
-- src:35485 | (b) procure a third person to subscribe for, purchase or sell, or
-- src:35486 | to enter into an agreement to subscribe for, purchase or sell,
-- src:35487 | the securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts or CIS
-- src:35488 | units mentioned in subsection (1).
@ref s 219(3) (src:35474-35488)
GIVEN
    `subsections (2) and (3) apply to the insider (the answer under section 219(1))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 219(1) answer for this person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `the insider communicated the information, or caused it to be communicated, directly or indirectly, to another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the insider, directly or indirectly, communicate the information, or cause it to be communicated, to another person?
    `the insider knows, or ought reasonably to know, that the other person would or would be likely to deal in or procure dealing in the securities, contracts or units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the insider know, or ought the insider reasonably to know, that the other person would or would be likely to subscribe for, purchase or sell, or enter into an agreement to subscribe for, purchase or sell, the securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units, or procure a third person to?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 219(3) the insider's communication of the information contravenes the bar` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `subsections (2) and (3) apply to the insider (the answer under section 219(1))` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to this Division, where" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [WHERE]
        IF `subsections (2) and (3) apply to the insider (the answer under section 219(1))` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether subsection (3) applies was not answered
        IF NOT `the insider communicated the information, or caused it to be communicated, directly or indirectly, to another person`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The insider must not, directly or indirectly, communicate the information" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN]
        IF `the insider knows, or ought reasonably to know, that the other person would or would be likely to deal in or procure dealing in the securities, contracts or units`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the insider knows, or ought reasonably to know" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [IF]

@ref s 219(3) (src:35474-35488)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 218 to s 219 prohibited act`
`s 219(3) the insider must not communicate the inside information to a person likely to deal` MEANS
    PARTY Individual "the insider"
    SHANT `s 219(3) communicate, or cause to be communicated, inside information to another person who would be likely to subscribe for, purchase or sell, or procure a third person to`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the insider communicated the information, or caused it to be communicated, to a person the insider knew or ought reasonably to have known would be likely to deal or procure dealing (section 219(3))"

§ `s 220: not necessary to prove intention to use`

-- src:35494 | 220.—(1) To avoid doubt, in any proceedings against a person for a
-- src:35495 | contravention of section 218 or 219, it is not necessary for the
-- src:35496 | prosecution or claimant to prove that the accused person or defendant
-- src:35497 | intended to use the information referred to in section 218(1)(a) or
-- src:35498 | (1A)(a) or 219(1)(a) in contravention of section 218 or 219, as the
-- src:35499 | case may be.
@ref s 220(1) (src:35494-35499)
GIVEN
    `the proceedings are for a contravention of section 218 or 219` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings against the person for a contravention of section 218 or 219?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 220(1) the prosecution or claimant must prove that the accused or defendant intended to use the information in contravention` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are for a contravention of section 218 or 219`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is not necessary for the prosecution or claimant to prove that the accused person or defendant intended to use the information"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any proceedings against a person for a contravention of section 218 or 219"

-- src:35503 | (2) In any proceedings against a person for a contravention of
-- src:35504 | section 218 or 219, it is not necessary for the prosecution or claimant
-- src:35505 | to prove the absence of facts or circumstances which if they existed
-- src:35510 | would, by virtue of sections 222 to 230 or any regulations made under
-- src:35511 | section 341, preclude the act from constituting a contravention of
-- src:35512 | section 218 or 219, as the case may be.
@ref s 220(2) (src:35503-35512)
GIVEN
    `the proceedings are for a contravention of section 218 or 219` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings against the person for a contravention of section 218 or 219?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 220(2) the prosecution or claimant must prove the absence of facts that would preclude the act from being a contravention by virtue of sections 222 to 230` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are for a contravention of section 218 or 219`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is not necessary for the prosecution or claimant to prove the absence of facts or circumstances"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any proceedings against a person for a contravention of section 218 or 219"

§ `s 221: penalties under Division 3`

-- src:35518 | 221.—(1) A person who contravenes section 218 or 219, shall be
-- src:35519 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:35520 | exceeding $250,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:35521 | 7 years or to both.
@ref s 221(1) (src:35518-35521)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 221(1) the penalty on conviction for contravening section 218 or 219` MEANS
    Penalty OF 250000, 84, TRUE, 0  -- fine not exceeding $250,000; imprisonment not exceeding 7 years (84 months); "or to both"; no daily fine stated

@ref s 221(1) (src:35518-35521)
GIVEN
    `the person contravenes section 218 or 219 (the answer under the section that is contravened)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 218(2), 218(3), 219(2) or 219(3) answer for this person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 221(1) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes section 218 or 219 (the answer under the section that is contravened)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who contravenes section 218 or 219, shall be guilty of an offence" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN]

-- src:35523 | (2) No proceedings shall be instituted against a person for an
-- src:35524 | offence in respect of a contravention of section 218 or 219 after —
-- src:35526 | (a) a court has made an order against the person for the
-- src:35527 | payment of a civil penalty under section 232; or
-- src:35529 | (b) the person has entered into an agreement with the
-- src:35530 | Authority to pay, with or without admission of liability, a
-- src:35531 | civil penalty under section 232(5),
-- src:35533 | in respect of that contravention.
@ref s 221(2) (src:35523-35533)
GIVEN
    `a court has made an order against the person for the payment of a civil penalty under section 232 in respect of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court made an order against the person for the payment of a civil penalty under section 232 in respect of the contravention?
    `the person has entered into an agreement with the Authority to pay a civil penalty under section 232(5) in respect of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person entered into an agreement with the Authority to pay, with or without admission of liability, a civil penalty under section 232(5) in respect of the contravention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 221(2) proceedings for an offence in respect of the contravention are barred` MEANS
    IF `a court has made an order against the person for the payment of a civil penalty under section 232 in respect of the contravention` OR `the person has entered into an agreement with the Authority to pay a civil penalty under section 232(5) in respect of the contravention`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No proceedings shall be instituted against a person for an offence in respect of a contravention of section 218 or 219 after" -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
